    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming an instance — the prefix families",
      "prov:value": "**Four of the eleven instances here carry no prefix at all** — `agent-skills`,\n`detangle`, `kg-navigation`, `large-datasets` (measured 2026-09-21,\n`findDeclarationFile` over each directory).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming an instance — the prefix families",
      "prov:value": "It does not\nextend to `folio-assistant-*`. That ruling settled a live merge conflict —\n`main` had renamed the core instance `folio-assist-core` while a branch carried\nthe content core — which is why it is written down rather than left to be\nre-derived."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`holds` has FOUR values, not three",
      "prov:value": "`derived` is the newest and the one most often missed: it was added 2026-09-20\n(bean `hqku`) when `library/` turned out to be neither content nor context —\n*not* `context`, because `document-ingestion.bpmn` writes it and `context`\nmakes that a defect; *not* `content`, because a QA finding against a derived\nsection is a finding against its **generator**, and sends a reviewer to the\nwrong file.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean hqku",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`recordsWork` is narrower than `holds: \"state\"`",
      "prov:value": "It asks whether the graph records **work somebody is partway through**, not\nmerely whether something writes to it. The distinction was measured rather than\nassumed: reading it as \"declares any state graph\" made the repository root and\nthe IRIS replica ACTIVE on `uploads` alone, and an ingestion queue is live state that\nnobody is partway through."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where a kind may live — a layer owns the kinds it can render",
      "prov:value": "The rule in its true form is **a layer owns the kinds it can render** — not\n\"the harness owns no renderable kind\", which was the earlier phrasing and\nstopped being true the day the harness shipped a renderer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where a kind may live — a layer owns the kinds it can render",
      "prov:value": "**Registration on import is for a kind that may legitimately be ABSENT.** A\nfirst attempt registered `docs` on import too, mirroring `folio`, so that the\nsentence *\"the harness's own vocabulary contains no renderable kind\"* could stay\nliterally true."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`bootstrap/README.md` is the first one",
      "prov:value": "It is the page a Bootstrapping Agent reads before it knows anything — *\"you have been\npointed at a repository, you know nothing about it\"* — and it is written for\n**this** repository. Measured 2026-09-21: it resolves **13 links into\n`../cat-harness/`**, across **6 distinct files**:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you push",
      "prov:value": "`bun run cat gates` is the one to run, and it is stronger than \"a list someone\nmaintains\" in two distinct ways worth knowing before you trust it (bean `j2w4`):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean j2w4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you push",
      "prov:value": "The second half is what makes the first safe to rely on, and it was added\nbecause a CI failure went red on a gate the local runner had just passed."
    }
